#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# security-scan - check cached sources of all recipes for security findings
# without rebuilding (SECURITY.md groups F4/F6).
#
# For each recipe with a cache entry, extracts the cached source archives and
# scans the source tree:
#   * B_SRCGUARD - static grep for suspicious build-script patterns
#   * B_VULNSCAN - osv-scanner over lockfiles/manifests (via the Docker base
#     image, which is the only place osv-scanner is installed)
#
# Note: during builds the build script only scans the staged package tree
# (what ships) with syft + osv-scanner. This tool complements that by giving
# build-tree-wide visibility (dev dependencies, vendored test deps) without
# failing builds.
#
# Findings are filtered against the recipe's existing [SECURITY] section
# (vulnscan-ignore= / srcguard-ignore=), so only *new* findings are reported,
# in the same copy-pasteable [SECURITY] format the build script logs.
#
# Caveats:
#   * The cache holds the downloaded source, not the full build tree; findings
#     generated during the build (node_modules, generated Makefiles, lockfiles
#     created by npm install/go get/cargo when not committed) are not covered.
#   * Recipes without a cache entry (never built) are skipped and reported.
#   * The cache holds the last fetched version, which may differ from the
#     current recipe version.
#
